<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Malmö (1803)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Malmö of 1803 was an agreement by which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> pawned the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wismar">Wismar</a>, with the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poel">Poel</a> and the district of Neukloster, to the Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin for 1,250,000 riksdaler for 100 years. Sweden never redeemed the pledge, and in 1903 it formally renounced its rights, so Wismar remained part of Mecklenburg.</p></div>
